  "legalPrivacyPushTitle": "Push notifications",
  "legalPrivacyPushBody": "If you turn on notifications in the iOS or Android app, we let you know when a new episode arrives — all new episodes, or only from the channels you choose on the Notifications screen. Delivery uses Google Firebase Cloud Messaging: your device receives a registration token and subscribes to the topics you chose (such as \"all new episodes\" or a single channel). We do not store the token or the topic list with your account; your choice of topics is kept only on your device, and Google holds the subscriptions as a data processor.\n\nWe send notifications on the basis of your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you give by turning notifications on and granting the system permission. You can withdraw it at any time on the Notifications screen or in your device settings. We do not send notifications between 10 pm and 7 am.",
